	OnikiriTutorialLead: {
		AskTitle: View the Tutorial?
		AskBody: Vigor & Stance, Omote & Ura forms of the domain, and the dismemberment backlash mechanism: understanding these beforehand helps avoid trouble in combat. This prompt appears only once
		AskPrompt: Click "Start Tutorial" to learn; skip if in a hurry; or accept the Keiko Rune to open the tutorial anytime later
		RefreshAskTitle: Tutorial Content Updated
		RefreshAskBody: This update adds two guides: how to consult the Mei Codex beside the Inscription Stand, and cautions before expanding the domain. Practiced steps will not repeat
		RefreshAskPrompt: Click to view the new content, or accept the Keiko Rune to check later
		AcceptBtn: Start Tutorial
		DeclineBtn: Not Now
		DeclineNotice: The Keiko Rune has been placed in your inventory; use it anytime to reopen the tutorial
		HudTitle: Vigor & Stance
		HudBody: While holding Onikiri, the lower-left HUD displays two status gauges. Vigor feeds Flash Step and Sakura Flight and refills over time; Stance builds by hitting enemies, unlocking tier executions at half and full gauge. Detailed move explanations can be viewed on the weapon tooltip
		HudPrompt: Check the status gauges in the lower-left corner and click "Understood" to continue. Click the sealing talisman to open the panel
		SigilTitle: Sigil Wheel
		SigilBody: Click the Sigil Wheel tab on the upper-left of the Inscription Stand to switch to this interface. The outer ring displays recorded wraiths, and the inner triangle has 3 binding seats. Click a wraith on the outer ring, then click an empty seat to bind it. Bound wraiths grant battle buffs, but each use increases revival and erosion. Click the scroll below to open the Ghost Register
		SigilPrompt: Click the highlighted upper-left tab to switch to the Sigil Wheel and view the outer ring and 3 binding seats
		MeiTitle: Inscription Stand
		MeiBody: Click the highlighted sealing talisman (or press hotkey) to open the Inscription Stand. Onikiri has three inscription slots: Tang, Groove, and Horimono. Each inscription grants a special effect and carries a cost. Click a slot to select a chisel; chisels in your inventory are listed in the tray below
		MeiPrompt: Press {0} or click the highlighted talisman to open the stand and inspect the three inscription slots
		CodexTitle: Mei Codex
		CodexBody: Beside the Inscription Stand lies a booklet known as the Mei Codex. The left page categorizes all inscriptions by Tang, Groove, and Horimono; the right page displays effects, costs, and provenance. Unlocked inscriptions show affinity progress. Read-only; chiseling is still done at the stand
		CodexPrompt: Click the highlighted booklet on the right to open the codex; closing it returns to the stand
		DomainTitle: Eye of the Oni Domain
		DomainBody: The eye beside the Vigor gauge represents domain status: expand into the shallow "Omote", flip into the deep "Ura", or close the domain. Onikiri's core "Dismemberment" execution can only be triggered in Ura
		DomainPrompt: Left-click the eye to expand or close the domain; Right-click or press {0} to flip between Omote and Ura
		PrepareTitle: Practice Preparation
		PrepareBody: Please close any open interfaces and hold Onikiri. If the domain is already expanded, the system will automatically close it and reset to the initial tutorial state
		PreparePrompt: Keep Onikiri in hand and wait for the domain and UI to reset; if unresponsive, click "Skip" to proceed directly to practice
		OpenDomainTitle: Expand Omote
		OpenDomainBody: Press the Domain Expansion key (Q by default) to open the domain. When closed, pressing it enters the shallow "Omote", covering the world in yellowed paper style
		OpenDomainPrompt: Press {0} to expand the domain, and wait for it to stabilize in Omote
		FlipDomainTitle: Flip to Ura
		FlipDomainBody: While in Omote, press the Domain Flip key (middle mouse by default) to flip into the deep "Ura", turning the visuals into an ink-wash style
		FlipDomainPrompt: Press {0} to flip into Ura and wait for the visuals to stabilize
		DismemberTitle: Dismemberment Practice
		DismemberBody: In Ura, aim the cursor at the highlighted practice target, release left-click, then press it once more. Onikiri will dash forward and dismember the target body directly (hitting spawned Omokage paper also triggers dismemberment)
		DismemberPrompt: Aim at the highlighted target, release left-click, then press left-click again to dismember
		BacklashTitle: Endure Backlash
		BacklashBody: Directly dismembering an enemy body causes the wielder to suffer true backlash damage equal to 25% of max life, and briefly immobilizes you until the sheathing animation finishes (dismembering via Omokage paper has no backlash). Health will be restored after this step
		BacklashPrompt: Wait a moment for the sheathing animation to finish and health to restore
		CloseDomainTitle: Close the Domain
		CloseDomainBody: Practice complete. Lastly, close the domain. Left-clicking the highlighted eye on the HUD quickly closes the domain; pressing the Domain Expansion key again also closes it
		CloseDomainPrompt: Left-click the highlighted eye (or press Domain Expansion) and wait for the domain to close completely
		DomainUnboundHint: Domain Expansion key is not bound. You can press Q as a temporary default for this tutorial
		FlipUnboundHint: Domain Flip key is not bound. You can press Mouse3 (middle mouse) as a temporary default for this tutorial
		WaitingFeedback: Waiting for the action result to register
		BusyFeedback: The domain is transitioning forms; please wait until stable
		RetryFeedback: The action did not hit the target. Follow the prompt and try again, or click "Demonstrate"
		NeedBladeHold: Onikiri is not in your inventory. Put it in your inventory to continue
		TargetStalledHint: Practice target spawn location obstructed. If crowded, move to an open area and wait
		AssistBtn: Demonstrate
		RetryBtn: Retry
		NextBtn: Understood
		OpenSigilBtn: Open Wheel
		OpenMeiBtn: Open Stand
		OpenCodexBtn: Open Codex
		SkipBtn: Skip
		SkipStepBtn: Skip Step
		AbortBtn: Close Tutorial
		SkipAllBtn: Skip Tutorial
		SkipAllNotice: Tutorial skipped; trial commissions are now unlocked
	}

	OniMeiCodexUI: {
