OnikiriOverride: {
	DisplayName: Onikiri
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Hold left-click to drive the five-beat Crimson Rend combo; landing hits builds Stance
		Vigor fuels Flash Step and Sakura Flight; half and full Stance each unlock a tier of execution
		'''
	KeyLabelFlashStep: Kamui Flash Step
	KeyLabelSakura: Sakura Flight
	KeyLabelExecute: Execute
	KeyLabelDomain: Domain Expansion
	KeyLabelFlip: Omote/Ura Flip
	KeyLabelTeleport: Domain Teleport
}

OnikiriTrialQuestLine: {
	QuestCategory: Onikiri · Trial Cuts
	TrackerWaiting: It isn't here yet. Wait, or we go ask for it
	TrackerFighting: "{0}: {1:0%}"
	TrackerBrief: Next cut: {0}
	BossRushTargetName: Battle of Terminus
	EventActiveFormat: "{0}: underway"
	Trial_0: Skybound Eye
	Trial_1: Twain Evils of the Soil
	Trial_2: Clustered Blight
	Trial_3: Presumptuous God
	Trial_4: The Dividing Flesh
	Trial_5: Pus-Rotten Scales
	Trial_6: Ashes in the Abyss
	Trial_7: Roaring Metal Serpent
	Trial_8: Twin Demon Eyes
	Trial_9: Mingled Remains
	Trial_10: Mimicked Silhouette
	Trial_11: Bloom in the Depths
	Trial_12: Temple Golem
	Trial_13: Mad Chant at the Gate
	Trial_14: Looming Pale Moon
	Trial_15: Corefire Radiance
	Trial_16: Phantasmal Cluster
	Trial_17: Void Devourer
	Trial_18: Lingering Fire Dragon
	Trial_19: Deafening Exo-Steel
	Trial_20: Stifling Calamity
	Trial_21: Recurrent Darkness
	TrialSummary_0:
		'''
		Always feels like something is watching from the dark sky above, and the blade shivers in my hands
		I cannot say for certain what it is, climb up into the night sky and take a look
		Do not keep your head craned up forever or your neck will ache, tell me what you saw when you are back
		'''
	TrialSummary_1:
		'''
		The wind blowing from the corrupted soil carries two foul odors, heavy and rank, even I cannot tell them apart
		If you cross paths with them, deal with whichever lunges first, do not let yourself get surrounded by both
		Draw your blade the moment the air turns sour, finish up quick and come back out to breathe
		'''
	TrialSummary_2:
		'''
		Deep underground that cluster of filth has gathered into a den, smells slimy and nauseating even from afar
		Leaving it alone will only let it fester deeper, go scatter it once and for all
		Watch your step in the mud, do not come back splattered all over
		'''
	TrialSummary_3:
		'''
		I hear people say some heap of sludge over there claims to be a god, it almost made me laugh
		If taking divine titles were that easy, who would bother training and cultivating?
		Go see what it can actually do, if it is only pretending to be a spirit, pierce it with a single cut
		Listen carefully now, you are going there to pierce it, do not be foolish enough to kneel and worship
		'''
	TrialSummary_4:
		'''
		Deep down near the bottom of the world a colossal wall of flesh has blocked the road shut, even cutting through the air feels stifling
		When the road is shut, the only answer is to cleave it open
		Once this fight is through the world around will likely shift, stay sharp, we will talk when you make it past
		'''
	TrialSummary_5:
		'''
		There is huge commotion beneath the dunes, sand churning endlessly as if some great worm is boring straight down
		Cut it off before it burrows too deep
		Watch where you plunge the blade, do not shove the whole hilt into the sludge, I live in here too, leave me some clean space
		'''
	TrialSummary_6:
		'''
		The fire pit over that way is still glowing red, the blade feels scorching even from this distance
		Go put it out, no sense letting it burn forever
		Mind your footing across the magma shoals, no one is going to blow on your soles if you get burned
		'''
	TrialSummary_7:
		'''
		The tremors from beneath the earth are growing louder by the beat, the blade is vibrating with them, sounds like a giant clanking with iron
		A terrifying title changes nothing, iron is still iron, go test how thick its hide really is
		Do not clash head-on against solid metal, aim for the seams so your hands do not go numb
		'''
	TrialSummary_8:
		'''
		Two glares in the night sky like they agreed to rise together, being watched from both sides feels awful
		They cover each other well when paired up, pull some distance and take them down one by one, do not get caught in the crossfire
		Go on, be quick about it, tell me what they look like once you are back
		'''
	TrialSummary_9:
		'''
		The aura drifting from that way feels strange, iron frames bolted to ancient bone, half-baked and mismatched
		No matter how large the scaffolding is, it is still pieced together, do not let its silhouette bluff you
		Strike at the joints where it connects, take it apart piece by piece, then tell me which part was real
		'''
	TrialSummary_10:
		'''
		A shadow up ahead walks far too much like a living person, yet carries not a shred of human warmth
		Counterfeits that mimic human gait are the most treacherous, do not stand there staring it in the eyes
		Step forward and shatter that false shape, we will talk about who it was copying after it is done
		'''
	TrialSummary_11:
		'''
		A sweet scent is rising from beneath the jungle, smelling sickly and rotten underneath
		No matter how pretty a blossom looks, once the core rots away it must be pruned, lest it foul the whole thicket
		I can teach you the ways of flower pruning when you return, go on, watch out for the creeping vines
		'''
	TrialSummary_12:
		'''
		A massive stone idol sits inside the temple refusing to budge, looks dense and stubborn
		Find a way to topple it and break the joints, do not bash the blade against solid rock, chipping the edge hurts me too
		If your wrists get shaken numb, shake them out properly once you are back
		'''
	TrialSummary_13:
		'''
		A flock of robed figures outside the dungeon muttering gibberish without end, my ears are exhausted just listening
		Go over and cut their chanting short, spare us both the racket
		Whatever nonsensical scripture they are reciting, do not believe a single syllable, finish up and come back soon
		'''
	TrialSummary_14:
		'''
		A massive canopy of gloom feels pressed against the sky above, looking up suffocates the chest
		If it hangs there in the way, fly up and strike it down
		Do not just stand beneath it spacing out, take it seriously, I will ask how tired you are once you return safe and sound
		'''
	TrialSummary_15:
		'''
		Waves of heat keep rolling up from the core of the earth, the steel I rest in is already burning hot
		Getting close on this run will be scorchingly painful, keep that in mind beforehand
		Do not drag things out in the blistering heat, strike true and pull back immediately
		'''
	TrialSummary_16:
		'''
		The damp depths are swarming with a knot of wandering spirits, too many for me to even bother counting
		Since they are all tangled together, do not bother picking them off one by one, sweep the whole clump in a single stroke
		The dungeon is freezing cold and damp, do not stay down there too long, finish the job and come back up
		'''
	TrialSummary_17:
		'''
		That direction feels completely hollow, my heart sinks just looking into it, the blade is dragging heavy too
		I cannot say what kind of titan is coming our way, keep your guard up
		Do not freeze in awe when you get there, no matter how dire it looks, coming back alive matters more than anything
		'''
	TrialSummary_18:
		'''
		They say one stubborn dragon still remains at the edge of the ash sea, go see whether the rumor holds true
		Once blades cross the steel will likely burn red-hot, bear with it
		I do not care about rare dragon scales or feathers, just come back in one piece
		'''
	TrialSummary_19:
		'''
		Can hear the iron cannons thundering from leagues away, my head is throbbing from the racket
		Go silence those mechanical monstrosities, protect your ears on the way
		If your ears are still buzzing when you return, I will find a quiet hollow for you to rest
		'''
	TrialSummary_20:
		'''
		The air over that way is sticky and stagnant, taking a single breath feels like choking on lead
		Go cleave through it, do not stand idly in the storm breathing in all that stifling smog
		Once you are back safe, I will teach you the breathing rhythms from my homeland
		'''
	TrialSummary_21:
		'''
		Those fallen shadows keep clustering back together as if they can never be purged clean
		This engagement is going to drag on for a long while, swing freely, I will be right here watching over you
		Plant your feet firm before you strike, when you return victorious I will nag you about whether you wobbled
		'''
}

KikasaOverride: {
	DisplayName: Kikasa
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Hold left click to hover the umbrella overhead, dropping homing ink rain to a steady beat
		Hold right click to charge ink upside down; release to pour out an ink torrent
		Rain and torrents you command by hand stamp an Ink Seal; your summons deal bonus damage to sealed targets
		'''
	GhostCountLine: Minion slots {0} · {1}
	TierName0: Drizzle
	TierName1: Side Toss
	TierName2: Volley
	TierName3: Lake Tilt
	KeyLabelDomain: Domain Expansion
	KeyLabelSink: Sink into the Lake
	KeyLabelMutate: Flip the Lake
	KeyLabelWheel: Shade Wheel
	KeyLabelRestart: Self-Restart
	KeyLabelTeleport: Domain Teleport
	KeyLabelPanorama: Lakeheart
	MutateFallback: Middle Mouse
}

KikasaTrialQuestLine: {
	QuestCategory: Kikasa · The Sinking Feast
	TrackerWaiting: Not seated yet—go invite it, or wait a while
	TrackerFighting: "{0}: {1:0%}"
	TrackerBrief: Next course: {0}
	BossRushTargetName: Battle of Terminus
	EventActiveFormat: "{0}: In progress"
	Trial_0: Soft First Course
	Trial_1: Night-Staring Eye
	Trial_2: Foul Soil Morsels
	Trial_3: Festering Depths
	Trial_4: Sweet Nectar and Stubborn Hooves
	Trial_5: Old Bones at the Gate
	Trial_6: Motley God-Gel
	Trial_7: Flesh Across the Path
	Trial_8: Winged Pink Gel
	Trial_9: Golden Drool in Rotten Sand
	Trial_10: Three Tastes of Iron
	Trial_11: Crimson Bloom of the Jungle
	Trial_12: Crystal-Shelled Morsel
	Trial_13: Temple Boulder
	Trial_14: Wave-Stirring Winged Boar
	Trial_15: Nocturnal Radiance
	Trial_16: Chanting at the Portal
	Trial_17: Moonback Reflection
	Trial_18: Kinfolk at the Table
	Trial_19: Ancient Acid-Bather
	Trial_20: Void Serpent Beyond
	Trial_21: Unquenched Blazing Plume
	Trial_22: Peak Iron and Peak Flame
	Trial_23: The Full Table Feast
	TrialSummary_0:
		'''
		A soft puddle of blue slime sits shivering endlessly at the foot of the mountains
		Puffed-up bulk gathered from who knows where, nothing more than empty bluster
		Go scatter it to pieces, do not let it block the road
		'''
	TrialSummary_1:
		'''
		A giant eyeball hangs in the night sky, staring without manners
		Does not even blink, enough to make skin crawl
		Go knock it down, once its eye is shut, it saves a world of annoyance
		'''
	TrialSummary_2:
		'''
		Two abominations burrowing from the rotten soil, one long worm and one soggy brain
		Can smell their rank mire stench from miles away
		Deal with whichever crosses your path first, cut them down and do not come back soaked in foul odor
		'''
	TrialSummary_3:
		'''
		A festering nest of rotten meat lies beneath the earth, crawling with blood-boring maggots
		Leaving it alone only lets the rot run deeper, go smash it apart
		Keep your gloves on tight, that sludge is impossible to wash off skin
		'''
	TrialSummary_4:
		'''
		A venomous bee in the jungle, a stubborn deer in the snowfields blind in one eye
		Take down whichever you encounter first, their tempers are equally foul
		One carries a poison stinger, the other stomps with blizzards, do not get careless
		'''
	TrialSummary_5:
		'''
		An ancient skeleton hangs by the dungeon gate, clinging to his post after a lifetime of watching
		Old as he is, his obsession is heavier than an iron lock
		Break his watch, take the key, and let him rest in the soil
		'''
	TrialSummary_6:
		'''
		Purple and red sludge stirred together, yet bold enough to call itself a god
		Scattered and impure, it will never amount to anything grand
		Go break it apart and dissolve it, spares the ground from being fouled
		'''
	TrialSummary_7:
		'''
		A colossal wall of flesh spans across hell, blocking the road completely
		Feels scorchingly hot even through the umbrella curtain, stifling to breathe
		Pierce it through, if the world shifts on its head afterward, that is none of your concern
		'''
	TrialSummary_8:
		'''
		A soft pink slime hovers in mid-air, bringing an entourage even when marching to battle
		Dressed up so gaudily, putting on quite the show
		Bring her down, grand as the display is, it cannot withstand a single downpour
		'''
	TrialSummary_9:
		'''
		A giant worm bursting with festering blossoms burrowed from the dunes, dripping golden pus
		Looks nastier than things rotted in water, one breath up close is choking
		Go dispatch it, rinse the umbrella canopy clean before you return
		'''
	TrialSummary_10:
		'''
		Someone built three iron contraptions: a chain, searchlights, and a four-armed steel skeleton
		Reeks of raw iron, clanking and noisy
		Dismantle them one by one, do not let them swarm together
		'''
	TrialSummary_11:
		'''
		A giant crimson flower sleeps in the jungle depths, spreading vines far and wide
		Wake her and she lashes out with a terrifying temper, coiling around whatever moves
		Pull her up by the roots, if vines wrap around the umbrella, cut them clean off
		'''
	TrialSummary_12:
		'''
		A mantis shrimp lies beneath the shore, glistening with a crystalline shell, shedding layer after layer
		One punch from those claws can shatter the water, quite a commotion
		Let it shed its shell as it pleases, watch the punches carefully, do not take a blow unaware
		'''
	TrialSummary_13:
		'''
		A square-headed stone idol squats inside the temple, refusing to budge an inch
		Crafted with intricate mechanisms, yet crack it open and it is just an empty frame
		Tear it apart, no sense letting it squat there blocking the hall
		'''
	TrialSummary_14:
		'''
		A winged pig in the sea, learning to stir up storms like a man
		Does not even look in the mirror, the temper of water is not for a sea pig to command
		Shove it back into the deep, saves it from splashing about in front of my eyes
		'''
	TrialSummary_15:
		'''
		A radiant figure soaring through the night sky, painfully blinding in the dark
		I dislike glaring lights, straining to look at
		Slip in under the cover of night and rub that glow dim, do not provoke her in broad daylight
		'''
	TrialSummary_16:
		'''
		Someone mutters endless chants by the dungeon gate, swollen and exhausting to the ears
		Whatever he seeks to draw down from the void is no righteous path
		Interrupt that ritual, before the commotion grows too grand to contain
		'''
	TrialSummary_17:
		'''
		That colossal shadow behind the moon is finally descending, covered in eyes
		Staring down at the mortal realm for all these eons, it is time for an end
		Go scatter it to pieces, and take a good look at the moonlight tonight for me
		'''
	TrialSummary_18:
		'''
		A vast knot of vengeful spirits drifts deep in the dungeon, stitched and patched for centuries
		Kin to what I am in the end, weeping day in and day out, exhausting to watch
		Let them scatter once and for all, returning to silence is better than suffering down there
		'''
	TrialSummary_19:
		'''
		An ancient relic lies pinned beneath the Sulphurous Sea, sour all over, temper sharper than acid
		We crossed paths back then, and neither yielded half a step
		Go settle him for me, consider it settling an old score of mine
		'''
	TrialSummary_20:
		'''
		That massive serpent wheeling across the sky, they say it has swallowed gods
		What level a god reaches does not concern me, but circling overhead is dizzying to watch
		Bring it down, keep that sturdy carapace for yourself, pay no mind to the rest
		'''
	TrialSummary_21:
		'''
		A furious blaze has burned across the jungle for who knows how many centuries
		Fire and storm have never stood together since ancient times
		Go put out that fire, feathers soaked through will never lift again, as it should be
		'''
	TrialSummary_22:
		'''
		Two final brutal trials have met at once: an army of iron puppets and a witch bound by obsession
		Neither side is easily handled, leaving this realm not a single moment of quiet
		Take them in whatever order you prefer, dispatch the swiftest first, just walk out alive
		'''
	TrialSummary_23:
		'''
		Those fallen shadows have clustered together once more, or that ancient dragon in the abyss has awakened
		Whichever it is, the spectacle will not be small
		Grip the umbrella tight, take it one step at a time, once this fight ends... the rain outside should finally clear
		'''
}

KikasaText: {
	KikasaServantPlayer: {
		ServantUnknown: You can't command it yet
		AutoEvictFormat: Seats full — {0} steps down, {1} takes the seat
	}

	KikasaUIText: {
		AffinityFlame: Flame
		AffinityNightmare: Nightmare
		AffinityRain: Rain
		AffinityWild: Any
		AffinityArms: Arms
		StateOut: Out
